The bug was caused by the improper handling of memory thresholds in the memory control group (memcg) system, where thresholds were converted to bytes but were still being tracked in page units internally. This inconsistency led to potential overflow issues on 32-bit architectures, as the unsigned long type could not accommodate values exceeding 4G. The regression was further exacerbated by the incorrect return type and value manipulation in the `mem_cgroup_usage` function, which did not account for the necessary conversions when reporting memory usage and thresholds.

