Reason:
The fix involves returning the value directly in page units without shifting it to bytes, thus avoiding overflow issues. The threshold handling is also adjusted to ensure that thresholds are consistently managed in page units, which prevents the overflow problem on 32-bit architectures. This change ensures that the internal representation aligns with the user-facing representation, maintaining consistency and correctness.


